 ## Overview
-This method estimates the surface area of a solid by summing the areas of the triangular polygons produced by the marching cubes algorithm to approximate the solid's frontier [S1, book]. It differs from sibling methods by focusing on the aggregate geometric measure (area) rather than local vector properties like normals [1005-marching-cubes-surface-normal-estimation.md] or topological smoothing [1594-marching-cubes-smoothing.md]. While it provides a direct scalar estimate of the isosurface extent, it is known to lack multigrid convergence for standard linear implementations, meaning the error does not necessarily vanish as grid resolution increases [S1, book].
