 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs**
-- **Input**: The set of triangles $\{T_i\}$ generated by the marching cubes algorithm approximating the isosurface $V_h(S)$ of a solid $S$. Each triangle $T_i$ is defined by three vertices $p_1, p_2, p_3$.
-- **Output**: A scalar value representing the estimated surface area $A_{est} = \sum \text{Area}(T_i)$.
