 ## Background
-The method is described in the context of digital geometry and local polyhedrization techniques. It is discussed in the book *Digital Geometry* by Reinhard Klette and Azriel Rosenfeld (2004) [S1, book]. The analysis highlights the theoretical limitations of local methods like marching cubes for estimating geometric properties such as area and curvature, noting that these estimates often fail to converge to true values due to discretization artifacts dependent on grid orientation.
